WEBVTT

00:00.008 --> 00:35.166
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:57.875 --> 00:58.791
Everything okay?

00:58.875 --> 01:01.625
-Would you get this dry-cleaned?
-Sure thing.

01:01.708 --> 01:02.833
-Thanks.
-Thanks.

01:08.750 --> 01:10.125
You're amazing.

01:10.208 --> 01:11.250
Thanks.

01:11.958 --> 01:12.916
Let me see.

01:14.875 --> 01:16.208
You got it!

01:16.291 --> 01:17.750
You're a genius.

01:18.250 --> 01:19.083
Thanks.

01:20.833 --> 01:21.958
No sunflowers.

01:22.041 --> 01:24.416
And divide them among the tables. Thanks.

01:24.500 --> 01:26.583
-The kitchen's ready for you.
-Thanks.

01:44.166 --> 01:45.916
-Yes! Thanks.
-Thanks.

01:46.000 --> 01:49.458
There's a sprinkler issue.
Help is on the way.

01:49.541 --> 01:51.083
-How long?
-Five minutes.

01:51.166 --> 01:54.000
-The awnings are out. Looks amazing.
-Right.

01:55.291 --> 01:57.000
-It looks great.
-I know, right?

01:57.500 --> 01:58.666
It looks fantastic.

02:00.083 --> 02:01.333
Is that crooked?

02:01.416 --> 02:02.458
-The big one?
-Yes.

02:02.541 --> 02:04.916
No way. Lærke, everything's perfect.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.208
This opening's going to be
completely smooth.

02:07.708 --> 02:09.458
Oh boy, there's the boss.

02:09.541 --> 02:10.416
Yup.

02:12.166 --> 02:14.166
Wash this off before the VIPs arrive.

02:14.250 --> 02:16.166
Of course. I'll get it done.

02:29.083 --> 02:30.708
I'm trying to quit smoking.

02:32.791 --> 02:33.666
Sit down.

02:33.750 --> 02:35.583
No, everyone will be here soon.

02:35.666 --> 02:38.791
We've got a selfie wall.
That'll occupy them for an hour. Sit.

02:39.458 --> 02:40.333
Right.

02:42.208 --> 02:45.083
I want to talk to you about something.
Listen.

02:45.166 --> 02:47.416
So far we've bought
these rundown buildings,

02:47.500 --> 02:48.833
renovated them,

02:48.916 --> 02:50.833
put our logo on them, opened a hotel.

02:50.916 --> 02:52.416
Beautiful. So proud.

02:53.083 --> 02:56.583
But you've always wanted
to build something from scratch.

02:56.666 --> 03:00.916
And Weltzer has finally agreed to do it,
and I've found a brilliant place.

03:01.625 --> 03:02.791
It's in…

03:03.791 --> 03:05.000
Málaga.

03:05.083 --> 03:06.375
-Málaga?
-Yes.

03:06.458 --> 03:09.791
There's a former mango farm owned
by a Dane. He's broke.

03:09.875 --> 03:12.750
But he seems to be very attached
to the place.

03:12.833 --> 03:16.458
For five years, the neighbors have tried
and failed to buy it.

03:16.541 --> 03:17.916
That's where you come in.

03:18.000 --> 03:21.625
I want you to go down there
and persuade him to sell.

03:21.708 --> 03:23.291
Don't you have people for that?

03:23.375 --> 03:25.000
I want you to do it.

03:25.666 --> 03:27.625
It's always been your dream.

03:27.708 --> 03:29.916
I want a seat on the board. So…

03:31.291 --> 03:33.541
-When?
-Um… Now.

03:34.166 --> 03:36.250
-What do you mean by "now"?
-Right now.

03:38.000 --> 03:39.916
I can't do that. You know that.

03:40.000 --> 03:42.500
-I'm going on vacation with Agnes.
-Bring Agnes.

03:42.583 --> 03:45.083
-Stay a week.
-I promised we'd go to Bornholm.

03:47.291 --> 03:48.791
You're being serious?

03:48.875 --> 03:51.333
-Yes.
-Okay. It's just… Bornholm, really?

03:51.416 --> 03:52.750
But she loves Bornholm.

03:52.833 --> 03:54.125
I promised her.

03:54.208 --> 03:55.333
Well…

03:55.416 --> 03:58.750
-I'll do it after the vacation.
-But it has to be now.

03:59.750 --> 04:03.291
I haven't taken a vacation in three years.
If I cancel again--

04:03.375 --> 04:07.666
I want a seat on the board. The election's
in two weeks, so it has to be done now.

04:09.333 --> 04:12.583
And Bornholm's not going anywhere,
unfortunately.

04:13.125 --> 04:15.375
So go down there and soak it all in.

04:15.458 --> 04:16.958
Do what you're best at. Right?

04:18.250 --> 04:19.083
Yes.

04:19.166 --> 04:20.250
You'll go there

04:20.333 --> 04:22.250
and come up with a cool concept

04:22.333 --> 04:25.625
and build the greatest hotel
Weltzer has ever put their name on.

04:27.541 --> 04:28.916
This is your dream, Lærke.

04:46.208 --> 04:47.750
What crappy weather!

04:48.458 --> 04:49.333
Hi.

04:50.291 --> 04:51.916
-How nice. Thank you.
-Thank you.

04:53.250 --> 04:55.291
You're so frustrating!

04:55.375 --> 04:56.583
Is she very upset?

04:56.666 --> 04:59.416
It's just…
you can't just change the plans.

04:59.500 --> 05:02.125
She was excited to hang out with you.

05:02.208 --> 05:03.958
That's what we're doing.

05:04.041 --> 05:07.458
That's cute, but it's not really, is it?

05:07.541 --> 05:08.500
You'll be working.

05:08.583 --> 05:10.708
-How will you hide it?
-You know what Joan's like.

05:10.791 --> 05:12.500
I don't know what to do.

05:13.291 --> 05:14.166
Yeah.

05:16.791 --> 05:18.250
How's Vivi doing?

05:18.750 --> 05:21.000
I have some news about Vivi?

05:21.083 --> 05:22.500
Yes? She's dead?

05:22.583 --> 05:23.708
Aw, she's dead,

05:23.791 --> 05:25.125
and now you want me back.

05:26.166 --> 05:27.166
We're pregnant.

05:27.250 --> 05:29.333
She's pregnant. We're pregnant.

05:30.291 --> 05:32.250
I'm going back on the school intranet.

05:32.333 --> 05:33.166
With Vivi.

05:33.750 --> 05:35.666
Yeah, it's tough, but it's also…

05:35.750 --> 05:38.833
What can you do when you go younger,
you know?

05:38.916 --> 05:41.375
Or not younger in that way. Not really.

05:41.458 --> 05:44.250
-No more, please.
-No. Of course.

05:44.333 --> 05:45.875
-Is she coming or what?
-Yes.

05:45.958 --> 05:47.875
I need to tell you that she…

05:49.250 --> 05:52.291
She didn't get into the school
of architecture. Sadly.

05:52.375 --> 05:54.125
Wasn't the response due in August?

05:54.208 --> 05:56.625
They start then.
The letter came two days ago--

05:56.708 --> 05:58.000
Fuck!

05:58.083 --> 05:59.500
She should have called me.

06:00.500 --> 06:02.583
-She should have called?
-Damn!

06:02.666 --> 06:05.333
I should have called her.
Damn, I should have.

06:05.416 --> 06:06.416
You were working.

06:06.500 --> 06:07.916
-I'm an idiot!
-A bit.

06:08.000 --> 06:10.208
Never mind. When you get down there

06:10.291 --> 06:12.666
and want to do something nice for her

06:12.750 --> 06:15.041
because you're an idiot,

06:15.125 --> 06:18.125
and you work a lot,
so you want to pamper her, and…

06:19.750 --> 06:20.666
This is important.

06:20.750 --> 06:23.916
Pay close attention.
No matter what, do not let her drive.

06:25.583 --> 06:27.625
-Hi, sweetheart.
-Hi, sweetheart.

06:30.000 --> 06:32.083
Right. Have a nice trip.

06:32.166 --> 06:33.916
We'll be fine.

06:34.666 --> 06:36.166
-Say hi to Vivi.
-Sure.

06:37.625 --> 06:39.500
There's a door there. Bye.

06:40.125 --> 06:41.375
Have a nice trip.

06:44.375 --> 06:45.416
Love you.

06:49.416 --> 06:50.333
Hi, sweetheart.

06:54.958 --> 06:57.500
"Hi, Mom." "Hi, sweetheart."

06:57.583 --> 06:59.541
-To the airport, please.
-Sure.

07:08.708 --> 07:11.291
Dad told me about
the school of architecture. Sorry.

07:12.041 --> 07:15.500
-Reapply next year. Lots of people do.
-I don't want to talk about it.

07:19.250 --> 07:23.083
I thought the response was due
in August, that's why I didn't call, but…

07:26.416 --> 07:29.000
Will you act like this
the entire vacation?

07:29.083 --> 07:31.250
It's not a vacation! I'm not stupid!

07:31.333 --> 07:32.666
-Excuse me?
-But--

07:34.000 --> 07:37.333
I just wanted to ask.
This is my son, Elton.

07:37.416 --> 07:39.166
He wants to see the plane take off,

07:39.250 --> 07:40.958
but we got aisle seats.

07:41.041 --> 07:43.041
Had you booked a window seat?

07:43.125 --> 07:45.125
No, we didn't book window seats.

07:45.208 --> 07:46.541
We got random seats.

07:46.625 --> 07:48.041
Oh, that's a bummer.

07:48.125 --> 07:49.666
Yeah. So…

07:49.750 --> 07:53.250
I was hoping you might like to swap seats?

07:53.958 --> 07:56.333
No, thank you.

07:57.083 --> 07:58.875
-We're good.
-Okay?

08:02.875 --> 08:06.041
Elton's only three,
and he's visiting his dad in Spain.

08:06.125 --> 08:08.791
It's his first time flying,
so he's anxious.

08:08.875 --> 08:12.958
But we've booked these, so no.
We've booked and paid for the seats.

08:13.041 --> 08:15.166
-I don't care.
-No, stay there.

08:15.250 --> 08:17.541
I said, "No." These are our seats.

08:20.083 --> 08:21.291
Don't be sad, sweetie.

08:21.375 --> 08:23.958
It might do him good
to be told "no" for once.

08:24.041 --> 08:26.375
-Don't hit me!
-Have my seat.

08:27.041 --> 08:28.208
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

08:28.291 --> 08:30.500
-Thank you!
-Don't mention it.

08:30.583 --> 08:33.000
-So kind.
-Then all the kids get their way.

08:33.583 --> 08:35.125
Yes, exactly. Thanks.

08:35.208 --> 08:37.125
-Sure.
-We say "thank you" to the man.

08:41.791 --> 08:43.250
What an annoying person.

08:43.333 --> 08:45.208
You are so fucking unbelievable.

08:45.291 --> 08:48.625
Me? She's the annoying one.
She should've booked seats.

08:48.708 --> 08:50.291
It's not my fault…

08:51.375 --> 08:53.000
-It's not my fault that--
-Shh!

08:54.541 --> 08:56.791
-She could've booked--
-Do that one more time…

08:58.000 --> 08:59.833
She could've booked her own tickets.

09:00.583 --> 09:02.208
Set the iPad volume to maximum.

09:26.708 --> 09:28.875
Should we get some food at the house?

09:31.833 --> 09:33.375
And perhaps a glass of wine?

09:34.541 --> 09:35.791
Where are we staying?

09:36.375 --> 09:39.125
We're staying at a… finca.

09:39.208 --> 09:40.583
That's a… Yeah.

09:40.666 --> 09:41.708
I know what it is.

09:41.791 --> 09:42.625
Right.

09:45.916 --> 09:50.250
The owner's Danish,
and Joan arranged for us to stay there.

09:51.916 --> 09:53.416
Someone she hooked up with?

09:53.500 --> 09:55.083
I'm sure they've been screwing.

09:56.208 --> 09:57.333
Ew!

09:58.833 --> 09:59.791
What?

09:59.875 --> 10:01.250
Don't say "screwing."

10:01.333 --> 10:03.125
What? That's what it's called.

10:06.125 --> 10:07.250
They actually screw…

10:08.708 --> 10:10.041
a heck of a lot down here.

10:10.583 --> 10:12.833
Lots of screwing, you know?

10:13.333 --> 10:14.333
It's not my fault.

10:14.416 --> 10:16.791
That's not my decision. But they do.

10:16.875 --> 10:19.583
They love to screw,
especially in our area.

10:22.750 --> 10:24.625
Is the word you don't like "screw"?

10:26.791 --> 10:29.166
-Screwing here, screwing there
-Stop it!

10:29.250 --> 10:31.500
Screwing in my tummy-- That's gross!

10:56.041 --> 10:57.625
What are we doing?

10:59.291 --> 11:01.291
Just checking something.

11:05.500 --> 11:07.125
There we go. There.

11:14.208 --> 11:15.791
What the hell is this?

11:27.375 --> 11:28.375
That's this one.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.458
Oh, right.

11:35.583 --> 11:38.291
-I need to check something. Wanna come?
-No.

11:39.958 --> 11:41.541
Fine. I'll be right back.

11:50.083 --> 11:51.291
Jeez, it's hot here.

13:07.541 --> 13:09.583
-Hi!
-Hi!

13:12.000 --> 13:13.333
What are you doing here?

13:14.250 --> 13:15.500
What am I doing here?

13:20.458 --> 13:22.875
This is my place.

13:24.000 --> 13:25.625
-This is your place?
-Yes.

13:26.583 --> 13:27.583
Right.

13:29.916 --> 13:32.041
I was told it was a former mango farm.

13:32.125 --> 13:33.125
Orchard.

13:33.625 --> 13:34.708
Got it.

13:34.791 --> 13:37.208
This is our home,

13:37.291 --> 13:39.958
and the orchard is up and running.

13:40.041 --> 13:41.250
-Right.
-Yup.

13:42.708 --> 13:44.375
What can I do for you?

13:45.916 --> 13:47.500
It's really hot, isn't it?

13:47.583 --> 13:48.416
Yes.

13:49.583 --> 13:52.333
-I could do with a cold drink.
-Sure.

13:52.416 --> 13:55.125
Have a seat on the couch.
I'll be right with you.

13:55.208 --> 13:56.375
Right.

13:56.458 --> 13:57.583
When it's your turn.

13:59.708 --> 14:00.875
Yes, over there.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.541
Okay. Thanks.

14:16.791 --> 14:17.916
There you go.

14:21.666 --> 14:22.708
What?

14:23.416 --> 14:25.958
I've never seen
so many mango-based things before.

14:26.750 --> 14:28.500
It's a mango orchard.

14:28.583 --> 14:32.250
-There's a mangonade.
-No, it's pronounced mangonade.

14:34.333 --> 14:35.291
Mangonade.

14:37.875 --> 14:38.916
Like lemonade.

14:39.583 --> 14:41.708
But with mangoes instead of lemons.

14:41.791 --> 14:42.958
A mangonade?

14:44.708 --> 14:45.916
-Want one?
-Yes.

14:46.000 --> 14:47.458
-I've got to try it.
-Right.

14:48.208 --> 14:49.083
Thanks.

14:51.458 --> 14:52.541
Mangonade?

14:52.625 --> 14:54.583
Jesus Christ.

14:54.666 --> 14:55.625
Mangonade.

14:59.583 --> 15:00.541
Do you have Wi-Fi?

15:01.750 --> 15:04.250
Sure. We have 6G up here.

15:04.750 --> 15:05.708
No, I guess not.

15:05.791 --> 15:06.708
Never mind.

15:21.500 --> 15:24.791
Hi. Can I help you?

15:57.458 --> 15:58.291
Agnes.

16:42.208 --> 16:43.041
Thanks.

16:45.333 --> 16:46.333
Yes.

16:51.750 --> 16:52.708
Yeah.

16:54.041 --> 16:58.333
It's funny because
it's way too sweet and sticky,

16:58.416 --> 16:59.458
and the glass is…

17:01.083 --> 17:02.916
well, it's a disaster, but still…

17:03.541 --> 17:04.708
it works.

17:06.000 --> 17:07.375
It works. I'm impressed.

17:07.958 --> 17:09.458
Wow. Okay.

17:10.166 --> 17:12.875
-What?
-I've never heard anyone compliment--

17:12.958 --> 17:15.333
-Was it a compliment?
-Yes.

17:15.416 --> 17:16.916
And at the same time be so…

17:18.166 --> 17:19.291
rude.

17:20.083 --> 17:22.291
Isn't a compliment always nice regardless?

17:22.791 --> 17:24.458
-Is it?
-I believe so.

17:28.166 --> 17:29.333
You're cross-eyed.

17:30.208 --> 17:31.250
Excuse me?

17:34.333 --> 17:35.291
What?

17:35.375 --> 17:37.416
Your eyes… You're cross-eyed.

17:38.458 --> 17:39.500
No, I'm not.

17:39.583 --> 17:42.166
And that's rude, by the way.

17:42.250 --> 17:43.666
Yes, but it's very charming.

17:44.166 --> 17:45.333
It's a compliment.

17:46.000 --> 17:47.083
Okay.

17:47.916 --> 17:48.916
Funny. Really funny.

17:53.875 --> 17:55.166
Weltzer sent you, right?

17:57.375 --> 17:58.500
Yes.

17:59.791 --> 18:02.250
You've come a long way for nothing.

18:02.333 --> 18:05.125
I've made it clear that I'm not selling.

18:06.750 --> 18:09.958
Head back home
and sell some more waterfront houses.

18:11.000 --> 18:13.416
-I'm not a real estate agent.
-You look like one.

18:17.000 --> 18:19.166
You're rude. It's not nice to be here.

18:19.250 --> 18:20.583
Oh, well. Seven.

18:21.500 --> 18:23.250
-Seven?
-Euros for the mangonade.

18:23.333 --> 18:24.875
No problem. Coming right up.

18:26.708 --> 18:28.000
We only accept cash.

18:31.750 --> 18:35.083
Weird that you don't have
more customers with that service.

18:35.166 --> 18:38.375
-Lots of customers, but no change.
-Seriously?

18:38.458 --> 18:40.958
Yes. Find something in our mango shop.

18:41.041 --> 18:42.291
-No.
-Mango juice?

18:42.375 --> 18:44.875
-No more mango. I've had enough.
-Dried mango?

18:44.958 --> 18:46.625
-Definitely not.
-Mango jam?

18:46.708 --> 18:49.000
-You know what?
-Mango vinegar?

18:49.083 --> 18:51.333
It's not working, your mangonade.

18:51.416 --> 18:52.583
And the name sucks.

18:52.666 --> 18:54.291
-Mango beer?
-No, thank you.

18:56.041 --> 18:58.291
-Mango chutney?
-No, thanks.

19:09.291 --> 19:10.416
It's really good.

19:24.375 --> 19:25.333
Fuck.

19:27.583 --> 19:28.625
Agnes!

19:40.625 --> 19:41.458
Oh, God.

19:42.416 --> 19:46.750
Hi. Listen. My daughter wasn't in the car,
and I can't reach her.

19:46.833 --> 19:48.791
-No reception.
-Your daughter?

19:48.875 --> 19:49.791
Yes.

19:50.416 --> 19:51.750
The girl from the plane?

19:51.833 --> 19:53.041
Yes.

19:53.125 --> 19:55.250
-She's a big girl.
-I know, but--

19:55.333 --> 19:58.083
-She probably just went for a walk.
-Where would she go?

20:01.416 --> 20:02.583
Shit.

20:05.541 --> 20:06.416
Paula?

20:10.458 --> 20:11.833
-Are you there?
-What?

20:11.916 --> 20:12.916
This is Paula.

20:15.083 --> 20:16.583
Did you take a girl with you?

20:17.083 --> 20:18.166
Yes.

20:18.250 --> 20:20.875
You have to say "over"
when you're done speaking.

20:20.958 --> 20:21.875
Over.

20:26.958 --> 20:28.375
No problem, boss.

20:28.458 --> 20:29.750
We'll be there in five.

20:29.833 --> 20:31.333
Okay, thanks. It's fine.

20:31.416 --> 20:34.291
-She's gone for a drive with Paula.
-Who the hell's Paula?

20:34.375 --> 20:35.666
Paula's family.

20:35.750 --> 20:37.625
It's fine. They're on their way back.

20:42.500 --> 20:44.750
Is the fancy coffee only for fancy guests?

20:45.250 --> 20:47.291
That hasn't worked for years.

20:52.041 --> 20:53.000
Thanks.

20:55.166 --> 20:57.916
Don't take it personally.
We just don't need more…

20:58.708 --> 21:00.916
big, ugly hotels down here.

21:01.000 --> 21:04.083
Fortunately, we don't build ugly hotels.

21:04.166 --> 21:05.500
We have great taste.

21:11.125 --> 21:14.208
You've got
really shitty reception here, huh?

21:14.708 --> 21:17.208
Yeah. And we have
no running water at night

21:17.291 --> 21:20.333
from 11:00 p.m.
to 7:00 a.m. every morning.

21:20.416 --> 21:22.375
Inconvenient for watering trees.

21:22.458 --> 21:23.458
Yes.

21:23.541 --> 21:25.625
But fortunately all your friends

21:25.708 --> 21:28.916
who have built hotels
by the water have water 24-7.

21:29.000 --> 21:30.333
For their pools.

21:30.416 --> 21:31.625
Got it.

21:32.125 --> 21:34.875
-And Jacuzzis--
-My daughter's coming. I hear her.

21:34.958 --> 21:36.083
Fountains.

21:36.166 --> 21:37.333
Thanks for the coffee.

21:39.583 --> 21:42.541
-Where the hell did you go?
-Just went for a ride.

21:43.916 --> 21:46.250
You went for a ride.
You should've told me!

21:46.750 --> 21:47.875
Is it funny?

21:47.958 --> 21:49.750
-You acting like a mom?
-Funny.

21:49.833 --> 21:52.041
-What are you doing?
-What's going on?

21:53.041 --> 21:55.166
They're here to buy this place.

21:56.041 --> 21:58.166
Dude, you always think
the worst of people.

21:58.250 --> 21:59.416
It's the truth.

22:09.791 --> 22:12.916
Do I have to worry about
where you are the entire time?

22:13.416 --> 22:15.041
That's entirely up to you.

22:15.833 --> 22:17.750
Is it 'cause we didn't go to Bornholm?

22:18.250 --> 22:19.916
Are you punishing me for that?

22:21.708 --> 22:23.833
Just drop me off at the airport then--

22:23.916 --> 22:25.541
You're so childish.

22:26.750 --> 22:27.833
Forget it!

22:29.000 --> 22:30.000
Sit back.

22:55.666 --> 22:56.500
Damn.

23:00.916 --> 23:04.750
Agnes. Here. Take the key to the finca.

23:05.416 --> 23:08.000
-I dunno know where it is.
-It says "Casa Dona" on the door.

23:08.500 --> 23:10.916
-It's at the end of the street.
-They're stairs.

23:14.000 --> 23:15.791
Bornholm has many stairs.

23:17.458 --> 23:19.291
And The Sky Mountain and whatnot.

23:21.250 --> 23:24.333
Crazy amount of stairs.

23:36.125 --> 23:37.583
Want to order pizza?

23:37.666 --> 23:39.083
I'm not hungry.

23:39.166 --> 23:41.208
What? Come on. We haven't eaten all day.

23:41.708 --> 23:44.333
-I'm not hungry.
-How about burgers then?

23:46.916 --> 23:48.125
I'm going to bed.

23:48.833 --> 23:49.875
Fries?

23:51.125 --> 23:53.041
Or maybe some yummy pasta?

23:53.125 --> 23:54.291
I'm going to bed.

23:54.375 --> 23:55.250
Goodnight.

25:04.083 --> 25:09.500
THANKS FOR THE WINE.
I'VE LOOKED AT THE PROPERTY. CAN YOU TALK?

25:09.583 --> 25:11.750
SENT TO: JOAN

25:11.833 --> 25:14.291
LET'S TALK TOMORROW

25:26.375 --> 25:30.083
HOPE YOU HAD A GOOD FLIGHT. OUR BEEF
WELLINGTON GOT FIVE STARS. KRISTIAN

26:54.666 --> 26:55.500
Agnes?

27:10.708 --> 27:11.541
Agnes?

27:22.041 --> 27:22.916
Agnes?

27:58.958 --> 28:00.833
GONE TO TOWN, SEE YOU LATER.

28:00.916 --> 28:05.791
P.S. THE BALCONIES ON THE HOTEL NEED
TO BE STAGGERED FOR VARIATION AND RHYTHM!

28:11.916 --> 28:14.916
Hi. I thought you quit smoking?

28:15.000 --> 28:18.916
Yes, right.
So, what did you think of the place?

28:19.416 --> 28:20.875
The farm is still running.

28:20.958 --> 28:21.958
What do you mean?

28:22.750 --> 28:26.083
Well, it's a mango farm

28:26.166 --> 28:27.500
or mango orchard,

28:27.583 --> 28:28.416
as he calls it.

28:28.500 --> 28:30.333
We'll tear it down.

28:30.416 --> 28:33.166
There's water and electricity, yeah?
How's the internet?

28:33.250 --> 28:36.166
It's kind of non-existent,

28:36.250 --> 28:37.583
but that's practicalities.

28:37.666 --> 28:38.833
We'll fix that.

28:38.916 --> 28:40.250
The problem's the owner.

28:40.333 --> 28:42.583
He's annoying, and refuses to sell.

28:42.666 --> 28:44.000
Focus on the goal.

28:44.083 --> 28:45.791
Get to know him and persuade him.

28:45.875 --> 28:47.208
That's what you do.

28:47.291 --> 28:49.500
Yes, but it'll take longer than you want.

28:49.583 --> 28:51.416
-He's very--
-Are you with me or not?

28:51.500 --> 28:53.833
-We have a plan.
-Yes, of course.

28:53.916 --> 28:55.666
The board meeting is in 12 days.

28:55.750 --> 28:57.208
You'll find a way.

28:57.291 --> 28:58.625
-Yes.
-Ready, Joan?

28:58.708 --> 29:01.500
-Gotta go. Call if you need me.
-I'll figure it out.

29:01.583 --> 29:03.791
-I believe in you. Bye, sweetie.
-Bye.

29:13.125 --> 29:14.208
We have a deal.

29:14.291 --> 29:15.625
I'll pick it up next week.

29:16.125 --> 29:17.500
Sure. See you later.

29:17.583 --> 29:18.458
See you.

29:18.541 --> 29:19.666
Are you serious?

29:19.750 --> 29:21.041
Hey, beautiful. What?

29:21.125 --> 29:22.166
Are you serious?

29:23.000 --> 29:26.125
-We need the money, beautiful.
-But we also need the mangoes.

29:26.208 --> 29:29.750
Yeah, but I spoke to Hernando, and...

29:31.083 --> 29:33.708
We can use some
of his coches for the harvest.

29:36.333 --> 29:37.208
What?

29:38.666 --> 29:40.416
I don't know.

29:40.500 --> 29:44.041
I just feel like
I'm swimming upstream all the time.

29:45.833 --> 29:48.666
Don't you ever get tired of…

29:49.375 --> 29:50.916
swimming and swimming and…

29:51.958 --> 29:53.083
and nothing?

29:55.666 --> 29:56.666
Excuse me.

30:00.833 --> 30:02.166
Where are you going?

30:03.541 --> 30:05.333
Taking the Danish girl for a ride.

30:06.416 --> 30:08.500
-Dude.
-"Dude." What?

30:11.375 --> 30:14.250
We can't trust them, okay?

30:15.083 --> 30:16.000
You can't be trusted.

30:16.083 --> 30:17.708
-Yes, you!
-Me?

30:18.625 --> 30:19.458
Nice shirt.

30:20.500 --> 30:21.791
Thanks, sweetheart.

30:45.625 --> 30:46.916
Cross-eyed.

31:27.875 --> 31:30.666
-Shit! Jesus Christ.
-Hi.

31:32.125 --> 31:32.958
Hi.

31:35.416 --> 31:36.416
Who was that?

31:37.375 --> 31:38.666
Carlos and Dimitri.

31:38.750 --> 31:40.291
They own that hotel up there.

31:40.375 --> 31:41.958
Nice shirt. What did they want?

31:42.833 --> 31:44.125
-What did they want?
-Yes.

31:44.708 --> 31:48.541
The same as you. They've been trying
to buy me out for the past five years.

31:51.416 --> 31:54.208
-Would you show me around?
-Show you around?

31:54.291 --> 31:57.708
-No, we need to start harvesting.
-What were you doing in Copenhagen?

32:01.333 --> 32:03.041
-I told you.
-Come on.

32:03.125 --> 32:05.833
Nobody travels for four hours
to turn down an offer.

32:07.791 --> 32:08.708
Why did you go?

32:14.333 --> 32:17.333
I had a meeting with the bank
about a loan extension.

32:17.416 --> 32:18.500
They didn't grant it?

32:18.583 --> 32:19.750
-No.
-How much do you owe?

32:22.208 --> 32:24.083
We just need to bring in the harvest.

32:25.833 --> 32:26.791
I don't get you.

32:28.875 --> 32:30.333
I've been pretty clear.

32:31.291 --> 32:32.708
Okay? It's not for sale--

32:32.791 --> 32:33.916
What will you do?

32:36.625 --> 32:38.708
-I'll figure it out.
-No, you won't.

32:39.291 --> 32:42.958
You think this is a gold mine. It's not.
It's a run-down mango farm.

32:43.041 --> 32:45.166
-Orchard.
-Orchard. Whatever.

32:46.166 --> 32:47.958
You owe 4.9 million kroner.

32:48.583 --> 32:51.000
You have no savings and no assets.

32:51.083 --> 32:52.041
What's your plan?

32:56.166 --> 32:59.125
The plan is for me to work
and for you to go home.

33:00.041 --> 33:00.958
Okay?

33:02.625 --> 33:03.791
Thanks for stopping by.

33:23.416 --> 33:24.583
I'll just go down here.

33:24.666 --> 33:27.333
Hopefully, I won't fall
down the steep slope.

33:45.958 --> 33:46.958
A quick tour.

33:50.625 --> 33:51.625
Come on.

34:24.083 --> 34:25.083
Nice, huh?

34:26.041 --> 34:27.000
Yes.

34:27.708 --> 34:28.958
This place is…

34:29.875 --> 34:31.250
magical with that view

34:31.333 --> 34:35.250
and the constant northwesterly breeze
carrying the scent of--

34:35.333 --> 34:37.500
The scent of mangonade.

34:56.500 --> 34:57.375
We're here.

34:58.458 --> 34:59.416
Right. Yes.

35:03.166 --> 35:04.000
Thanks.

35:08.833 --> 35:10.541
This is the heart of the orchard.

35:11.458 --> 35:15.125
You've got the river that runs past
the house and down to the fields.

35:19.000 --> 35:20.000
All right?

35:26.708 --> 35:28.500
-When are they ready?
-Now.

35:29.166 --> 35:32.583
They bloom in the spring around April,
and they're ripe now.

35:34.083 --> 35:35.791
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

35:35.875 --> 35:36.916
It's not good.

35:40.166 --> 35:43.416
It takes six to ten years
for a tree to produce mangoes.

35:51.708 --> 35:53.000
-Hi.
-Hi, boss.

35:53.083 --> 35:54.083
All right?

35:59.875 --> 36:01.291
Was this always your dream?

36:03.541 --> 36:04.375
Yes.

36:04.458 --> 36:08.708
I've dreamed of starting a mango orchard
in Frigiliana since I was five.

36:08.791 --> 36:09.625
Really?

36:11.166 --> 36:12.416
No, you haven't.

36:15.916 --> 36:17.041
What was your job?

36:19.583 --> 36:20.833
I was a lawyer.

36:20.916 --> 36:21.958
A lawyer?

36:22.041 --> 36:22.875
Yes.

36:23.958 --> 36:25.750
Oh. Why did you stop?

36:28.750 --> 36:29.875
Was it love?

36:56.875 --> 36:58.041
It's not too bad.

37:05.125 --> 37:06.875
So it was love

37:06.958 --> 37:09.125
and then you two started a mango farm?

37:09.208 --> 37:10.375
-Orchard.
-Orchard.

37:10.458 --> 37:11.458
No, it…

37:12.708 --> 37:13.875
belonged to her family.

37:18.250 --> 37:19.500
-I have to work.
-Yes.

37:19.583 --> 37:21.166
Can you find your own way back?

37:21.916 --> 37:24.458
-Really?
-Left, right, left, and down the path.

37:24.958 --> 37:26.125
On the ATV?

37:26.208 --> 37:27.166
No!

37:27.666 --> 37:29.250
But it's a really nice walk.

39:47.333 --> 39:48.333
Still here?

39:51.250 --> 39:52.250
Have a seat.

39:54.125 --> 39:55.125
Have a seat.

40:04.750 --> 40:06.541
What if they can co-exist?

40:07.416 --> 40:09.541
-What can co-exist?
-Your mango f…

40:09.625 --> 40:12.000
-Orchard.
-…orchard and Weltzer's hotel?

40:13.083 --> 40:14.500
Just… Okay.

40:15.000 --> 40:18.250
If we preserve the fields,
the culture, and the trees.

40:18.333 --> 40:20.250
The hotel guests would love it.

40:21.458 --> 40:25.500
The hotel would bring life to the area
and create new jobs.

40:25.583 --> 40:28.416
Your staff would keep their jobs,

40:28.500 --> 40:30.708
you'd keep the place,
Weltzer would be happy.

40:30.791 --> 40:32.041
They'll pump money--

40:32.125 --> 40:34.625
You know there's no phone signal, right?

40:34.708 --> 40:36.750
I did notice that. I just think--

40:36.833 --> 40:39.000
Half the day, we don't have electricity.

40:39.083 --> 40:39.958
Yes.

40:40.041 --> 40:42.791
-No water at night.
-We'll fix it. Listen.

40:42.875 --> 40:45.250
If we solve the infrastructure issues,

40:45.333 --> 40:47.125
this would be mutually beneficial.

40:47.875 --> 40:48.708
Right?

40:48.791 --> 40:50.583
More activity, more jobs.

40:53.541 --> 40:56.208
Well? It's not completely stupid, right?

41:01.625 --> 41:06.500
Up, down, to the front, and inside!

42:06.041 --> 42:08.583
OWNERS DIE IN DEADLY FIRE

42:23.583 --> 42:28.375
LOCAL MANGO FARM DESTROYED
BY FIRE - BOTH OWNERS KILLED

42:32.583 --> 42:39.583
DANE SAVES GIRL FROM FIRE.
THE ONLY TWO TO SURVIVE.

43:21.250 --> 43:24.000
Before you freak out, I just want to say…

43:24.083 --> 43:25.083
Want some?

43:35.916 --> 43:36.750
Good, right?

43:38.625 --> 43:39.500
Yes.

43:42.625 --> 43:44.000
How was your day?

43:44.958 --> 43:46.916
Really nice, actually.

43:47.000 --> 43:48.250
-Really?
-Really.

43:50.125 --> 43:52.250
Paula introduced me to one of her friends.

43:53.166 --> 43:54.875
Then we went to a water park.

43:58.750 --> 44:01.166
-Not like kids. More like--
-No. Not like kids.

44:03.375 --> 44:05.666
Well, it actually was pretty childish.

44:05.750 --> 44:08.083
-That sounds lovely, sweetheart.
-It was.

44:11.041 --> 44:11.875
How about you?

44:11.958 --> 44:14.416
I went to the orchard again.

44:14.500 --> 44:15.500
So my legs hurt.

44:16.708 --> 44:17.583
Why go back?

44:17.666 --> 44:20.958
To find a way to build
that hotel for Weltzer.

44:22.708 --> 44:24.000
I saw your drawings.

44:24.083 --> 44:26.250
-Thanks for your input.
-You're welcome.

44:27.041 --> 44:29.291
But I doubt you'll get them to leave.

44:32.208 --> 44:33.041
Yeah.

44:34.541 --> 44:36.625
We've been invited to a party down there.

44:36.708 --> 44:37.833
No.

44:37.916 --> 44:39.541
I bet it's a mango party, right?

44:40.791 --> 44:42.083
Yes, I think it is.

44:42.833 --> 44:44.375
A fucking mango party.

44:47.583 --> 44:50.208
I'm sorry, I didn't know you got rejected.

44:50.291 --> 44:52.416
-Fuck it. It doesn't matter.
-No.

44:52.916 --> 44:54.000
It doesn't matter.

44:54.083 --> 44:55.250
It does matter.

44:56.000 --> 44:59.708
There's just been a lot going on lately.

45:02.541 --> 45:03.375
Right.

45:04.583 --> 45:05.833
-What?
-Nothing.

45:05.916 --> 45:07.083
No, tell me. What?

45:08.791 --> 45:10.333
A lot going on lately?

45:11.666 --> 45:13.625
Like, the past 18 years, or what?

45:26.958 --> 45:28.791
Do you remember your grandparents?

45:30.583 --> 45:32.250
Dad's mom and dad? Yes, I do.

45:32.333 --> 45:35.750
Yeah, that's what I mean.
Your dad's parents, but not my parents.

45:37.791 --> 45:39.541
I got something when I turned nine.

45:40.458 --> 45:44.208
I got a sticky note saying
they had gone to Munich,

45:44.291 --> 45:46.750
and they put me up with our neighbors,

45:46.833 --> 45:48.791
and came back for me a week later.

45:51.791 --> 45:52.958
Well, it's not…

45:53.041 --> 45:54.583
I mean, it's no excuse.

45:54.666 --> 45:56.291
But I'm just trying to say I…

46:01.041 --> 46:02.750
Your dad loves this kind of stuff.

46:03.791 --> 46:05.875
And he's so good at it.

46:05.958 --> 46:07.250
He's great at…

46:08.625 --> 46:12.541
Christmas, lunch boxes, and homework.

46:12.625 --> 46:14.041
And his parents--

46:14.125 --> 46:16.041
When I picked you up, I felt I was…

46:17.125 --> 46:21.166
tearing you away from your real family
and bringing you to a miserable apartment,

46:21.250 --> 46:22.666
where you'd scream for him--

46:22.750 --> 46:23.625
So it's my fault?

46:23.708 --> 46:25.166
No. It's not.

46:25.250 --> 46:27.791
I'm just saying that you had everything
at your dad's.

46:27.875 --> 46:28.958
At my place…

46:31.500 --> 46:33.333
there wasn't really anything at all.

46:36.333 --> 46:37.458
My mom was there.

46:48.125 --> 46:49.083
Yes.

46:57.791 --> 46:59.666
I'm sorry. That's so lousy--

46:59.750 --> 47:00.833
No, don't apologize.

47:00.916 --> 47:03.375
-That's shitty of--
-No, I hear you.

47:06.916 --> 47:08.041
I hear you.

47:20.958 --> 47:22.708
It's the weekend. Aren't you going…

47:24.250 --> 47:25.833
out with your new friends?

47:30.041 --> 47:31.500
No, I think they…

47:32.375 --> 47:34.000
They were tired and went home.

47:36.041 --> 47:38.666
-You can always wine up your mom then.
-Yeah.

48:17.625 --> 48:19.125
Paulita, give me a hand.

48:19.625 --> 48:20.458
Coming.

48:23.250 --> 48:25.500
-Are those from the southern end?
-Yes.

48:25.583 --> 48:28.583
Do you think we'll be able to use them
for the harvest party?

48:28.666 --> 48:29.625
I don't know.

48:30.375 --> 48:32.250
Did you invite the Danes?

48:32.791 --> 48:34.125
Yes, I invited Agnes.

48:37.166 --> 48:38.000
What?

48:40.208 --> 48:41.041
What?

48:43.041 --> 48:44.166
Dude, no way!

48:44.250 --> 48:45.875
-Yes, way.
-No!

48:45.958 --> 48:47.208
-Yes!
-Please.

48:47.291 --> 48:50.333
I saw you all fancy in your new shirt.

48:57.291 --> 48:58.541
Of course you don't.

49:03.000 --> 49:04.041
Alex?

49:04.125 --> 49:05.000
Yes?

49:07.291 --> 49:08.583
I wouldn't mind.

49:10.916 --> 49:13.875
I'm sure my sister wouldn't mind either.

49:13.958 --> 49:16.708
Actually, I'm sure
she'd be happy about it.

49:35.208 --> 49:37.375
What if both can co-exist?

49:37.458 --> 49:39.375
The mango orchard and Weltzer's hotel?

49:39.458 --> 49:42.750
If we preserve the fields,
the trees and the culture.

49:42.833 --> 49:45.041
The hotel guests would really love it,

49:45.125 --> 49:47.916
the hotel would revive the area

49:48.000 --> 49:50.000
and create more jobs for the locals,

49:50.083 --> 49:52.416
and we can build up trust

49:52.500 --> 49:53.708
while we're expanding.

49:53.791 --> 49:56.500
Anyway, I just wanted your opinion.

49:56.583 --> 49:57.500
Call me.

49:58.416 --> 49:59.250
Bye.

50:14.208 --> 50:15.541
What are you looking at?

50:16.750 --> 50:18.875
-What's up?
-What?

50:18.958 --> 50:21.000
Why don't you just ditch Joan?

50:21.083 --> 50:23.000
You're always making them money

50:23.083 --> 50:24.958
and doing everything for them.

50:25.041 --> 50:27.125
If you spent a fraction of that energy--

50:27.208 --> 50:29.041
Didn't you want to be an architect?

50:29.125 --> 50:31.250
Or was it a financial adviser?

50:35.041 --> 50:36.375
I'm my father's daughter, right?

50:39.333 --> 50:41.250
-Yeah.
-Talk to Dad about it.

50:41.333 --> 50:42.333
He would help you.

50:42.416 --> 50:44.625
-With what?
-Starting your own business.

50:46.125 --> 50:48.708
No, I'm not going solo.
Not when I'm on my way up--

50:48.791 --> 50:53.166
Stop! You have no boyfriend or friends,
you don't spend time with your family.

50:53.250 --> 50:56.458
-What more do you need?
-I think I have plenty of friends.

50:58.916 --> 51:00.541
When was your last boyfriend?

51:01.125 --> 51:02.000
When?

51:02.083 --> 51:02.916
Yes, when?

51:03.000 --> 51:05.000
I don't want to discuss that with you.

51:05.083 --> 51:06.291
Just tell me!

51:06.916 --> 51:08.458
When was it?

51:09.208 --> 51:10.958
-Dad?
-Yes. It was Dad.

51:11.041 --> 51:13.208
Yes. Your phone's ringing.

51:14.125 --> 51:15.166
Too bad.

51:15.250 --> 51:17.333
I don't mean to be a bitch. Just saying…

51:19.500 --> 51:21.083
My hands are wet. I can't.

51:22.000 --> 51:23.250
I do have friends.

51:24.041 --> 51:25.291
Hola, Paula.

51:44.750 --> 51:46.000
Want to drive?

51:46.875 --> 51:47.875
Really?

51:48.500 --> 51:49.583
Yeah.

51:49.666 --> 51:51.708
I don't get why Dad won't let me.

51:51.791 --> 51:53.833
I crashed his car like twice.

51:53.916 --> 51:57.125
-And then I'm banned for life.
-I'll just back it out.

51:57.208 --> 51:58.208
I know how to.

51:58.291 --> 51:59.333
I'll do it.

52:14.791 --> 52:16.166
-Stop.
-Really good.

52:17.583 --> 52:18.916
-Get your hand off.
-Great.

52:19.000 --> 52:21.458
-Stay in your own lane.
-I am.

52:21.541 --> 52:23.625
Yes, you are, but do it a bit more.

52:24.125 --> 52:26.625
-But I'm in the--
-Like that. This is fine.

52:31.416 --> 52:32.916
Am I cross-eyed?

52:33.916 --> 52:35.916
-What?
-Am I cross-eyed?

52:40.916 --> 52:42.083
Look at me properly.

52:51.250 --> 52:52.666
What the hell are you doing?

52:56.208 --> 52:58.333
Learn to drive, girl!

53:04.333 --> 53:06.000
-Can you drive?
-It's fine.

53:06.083 --> 53:07.125
Look forward--

53:07.208 --> 53:09.208
-I am.
-Eyes on the road. On the road.

53:19.125 --> 53:20.541
If you can drive here, then…

53:21.708 --> 53:23.125
then you can drive anywhere.

53:59.750 --> 54:00.583
Hi, Joan.

54:02.291 --> 54:03.375
Bad connection.

54:03.458 --> 54:04.625
Let me just get inside.

54:06.625 --> 54:07.875
What did you say?

54:07.958 --> 54:09.875
I just heard your message.

54:09.958 --> 54:10.875
What's going on?

54:10.958 --> 54:12.375
Do as you were told.

54:12.458 --> 54:16.500
Forget about the local community
and mango orchards.

54:16.583 --> 54:19.791
The board meeting's coming up
and this can't fail.

54:19.875 --> 54:22.916
You were supposed to convince him
and make him sign--

54:23.000 --> 54:24.458
Could you keep an open mind?

54:24.541 --> 54:26.083
Couldn't we try to maybe--

54:26.166 --> 54:29.166
Close the deal,
so we can tear down the mango farm.

54:33.166 --> 54:34.416
-Hello?
-I gotta go.

54:34.500 --> 54:35.375
-Bye.
-Hi.

54:36.125 --> 54:37.208
-Hi.
-Hi.

54:37.916 --> 54:38.958
I think there's a…

54:39.041 --> 54:40.083
Yeah, push.

54:40.166 --> 54:41.000
It's…

54:43.541 --> 54:44.500
Are you coming?

54:45.291 --> 54:46.958
Yes, all right. Yes, I'm coming.

54:58.208 --> 54:59.458
Jeez, it's hot.

55:15.500 --> 55:18.000
What's up, people?

55:19.875 --> 55:22.250
Holy Mary, we've eaten so many mangoes,

55:22.333 --> 55:24.125
we'll be sick to our stomachs!

55:24.208 --> 55:26.875
-What a party, right?
-Yes!

55:26.958 --> 55:29.166
Paula, I love you, beautiful.

55:30.458 --> 55:31.625
Here we go.

55:33.041 --> 55:36.708
I want to take a moment to talk
about a great friend of mine.

55:37.541 --> 55:40.208
A friend who looks out for all of us.

55:40.291 --> 55:41.666
Oh, Juan is at it.

55:41.750 --> 55:43.375
I have to tell you something.

55:43.875 --> 55:45.875
-Yes?
-If you've got a minute before.

55:45.958 --> 55:47.625
-Sure.
-Alex?

55:47.708 --> 55:51.791
Alex, Alex, Alex!

55:51.875 --> 55:55.166
I gotta go make a fool of myself now.

55:55.250 --> 55:56.583
No problem.

55:56.666 --> 55:57.875
-We'll talk after.
-Yes.

55:57.958 --> 55:59.333
-Grab a beer.
-Sure.

55:59.416 --> 56:03.708
Alex, Alex, Alex!

56:06.958 --> 56:09.208
Go, Alex, Go!

56:10.250 --> 56:12.791
Alex, Alex, Alex!

56:16.125 --> 56:18.208
It's a pleasure to have you all here.

56:18.708 --> 56:20.750
And I am certain

56:20.833 --> 56:23.125
that Ría, Manuel, and Mari

56:23.208 --> 56:24.625
would enjoy this very much.

56:25.625 --> 56:28.666
Mari especially would enjoy
hearing my clumsy Spanish.

57:00.583 --> 57:01.458
You?

57:36.166 --> 57:37.958
This community is my family.

57:55.041 --> 57:56.666
How do you say it, "Celebramos"?

57:56.750 --> 57:58.708
-Celebramos!
-Celebramos!

58:36.625 --> 58:37.541
A beer, please.

58:43.250 --> 58:45.333
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

58:52.500 --> 58:53.625
-What did you--
-What--

58:54.833 --> 58:55.666
You go first.

58:55.750 --> 58:57.166
I liked your speech.

58:57.833 --> 58:58.666
Thanks.

59:00.333 --> 59:01.958
I didn't mean any of it.

59:05.041 --> 59:06.750
What did you want to talk about?

59:08.541 --> 59:11.375
Nothing.

59:11.458 --> 59:13.458
It's not important.

59:19.291 --> 59:20.875
You really don't speak Spanish?

59:21.541 --> 59:22.875
You never picked it up?

59:22.958 --> 59:24.958
I think that was pretty good Spanish

59:26.916 --> 59:28.166
that I was just speaking.

59:29.750 --> 59:31.375
I think I speak it pretty well.

59:35.583 --> 59:38.708
-Hola.
-Hola, beautiful! I have to…

59:38.791 --> 59:39.708
Yes, of course.

01:02:07.041 --> 01:02:08.166
Hola? What's up?

01:02:28.750 --> 01:02:29.833
Coming.

01:02:31.666 --> 01:02:32.500
Hi.

01:02:32.583 --> 01:02:33.500
Hi. What's up?

01:02:33.583 --> 01:02:34.541
She's fine.

01:02:34.625 --> 01:02:35.750
-Yeah?
-The girls were…

01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:38.958
Or… they've had too much.

01:02:39.041 --> 01:02:39.875
Are you okay?

01:02:40.375 --> 01:02:42.250
-She's fine.
-Are you okay?

01:02:42.958 --> 01:02:44.625
There's something on your face.

01:02:45.541 --> 01:02:46.791
Come on, upstairs!

01:02:46.875 --> 01:02:49.000
-You got her?
-Come on.

01:02:49.083 --> 01:02:50.625
Get up. Get some sleep.

01:02:50.708 --> 01:02:52.583
-I can't…
-No, get up! Sweetie.

01:02:52.666 --> 01:02:53.875
-Okay.
-Grab her.

01:02:53.958 --> 01:02:55.500
Yes. Where's she going?

01:02:55.583 --> 01:02:56.583
Upstairs.

01:02:57.125 --> 01:02:58.791
-All right.
-Mind your head.

01:02:59.291 --> 01:03:01.250
It's the door back there.

01:03:01.333 --> 01:03:02.416
Right.

01:03:02.500 --> 01:03:03.791
-There.
-Got her?

01:03:03.875 --> 01:03:05.791
Yes. There, sweetie.

01:03:15.875 --> 01:03:17.333
Let's get her shoes off.

01:03:17.833 --> 01:03:20.416
There, there.

01:03:29.791 --> 01:03:30.625
Thanks.

01:03:37.083 --> 01:03:38.166
A glass of wine?

01:03:39.958 --> 01:03:40.916
Yes, please.

01:03:42.083 --> 01:03:44.291
-Were they on the plane?
-Yes. But--

01:03:44.375 --> 01:03:46.166
They were on the plane?

01:03:46.250 --> 01:03:48.250
Yes, they were on the plane.

01:03:48.333 --> 01:03:49.291
On a real plane?

01:03:49.375 --> 01:03:50.250
Yes. A small one.

01:03:50.333 --> 01:03:51.625
-No!
-Yes.

01:03:52.125 --> 01:03:53.000
A small plane?

01:03:53.083 --> 01:03:56.916
And they weren't…
I mean, they weren't going to take off.

01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:59.541
-It was definitely Paula's idea--
-It wasn't.

01:03:59.625 --> 01:04:00.500
I promise--

01:04:00.583 --> 01:04:01.791
I'll bet it was my--

01:04:01.875 --> 01:04:02.916
-No.
-Definitely!

01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:03.833
Listen.

01:04:03.916 --> 01:04:06.333
Paula thinks it's a secret,

01:04:06.416 --> 01:04:09.666
but she wants to become a pilot.

01:04:11.500 --> 01:04:12.333
So it was Paula.

01:04:17.375 --> 01:04:18.208
Okay.

01:04:19.708 --> 01:04:22.416
-I doubt it.
-She told me about her project.

01:04:23.166 --> 01:04:24.041
Project?

01:04:24.750 --> 01:04:27.166
Yeah, the one rejected
from the application.

01:04:28.416 --> 01:04:30.208
-She told you about that?
-Yes.

01:04:30.291 --> 01:04:32.333
It would've probably made more sense

01:04:32.416 --> 01:04:34.833
if she hadn't had half a bottle of rum--

01:04:34.916 --> 01:04:37.083
-Yes, I'm sure.
-But she's clever.

01:04:37.166 --> 01:04:38.166
Really clever.

01:04:40.625 --> 01:04:42.541
No wonder you're proud of her.

01:04:43.791 --> 01:04:45.583
She hasn't told me anything.

01:04:48.166 --> 01:04:49.208
About the project.

01:04:49.875 --> 01:04:52.083
I don't really know anything
about it, but I…

01:04:54.041 --> 01:04:55.666
haven't exactly asked either.

01:05:09.708 --> 01:05:12.625
-What about you?
-What about me?

01:05:12.708 --> 01:05:14.041
-What do you want?
-Me?

01:05:14.125 --> 01:05:15.375
What's your big dream?

01:05:15.875 --> 01:05:17.125
It's a big question.

01:05:18.208 --> 01:05:20.541
No idea. I haven't thought about it since…

01:05:20.625 --> 01:05:21.625
Since the fire?

01:05:38.208 --> 01:05:39.958
I remember that…

01:05:43.791 --> 01:05:45.041
I felt like…

01:05:47.166 --> 01:05:50.291
everything had been taken away from me.

01:05:51.000 --> 01:05:52.708
Everything I had,

01:05:53.208 --> 01:05:54.583
everything I loved,

01:05:55.208 --> 01:05:56.416
everything I believed in

01:05:57.500 --> 01:06:00.166
was taken away from me in a split second.

01:06:04.750 --> 01:06:08.041
But then I looked at Paula.

01:06:13.041 --> 01:06:16.958
This little, precious girl, who…

01:06:24.666 --> 01:06:25.875
She'd lost everything.

01:06:30.125 --> 01:06:31.666
So I think I just…

01:06:36.083 --> 01:06:38.041
I started rebuilding the farm,

01:06:38.541 --> 01:06:40.291
and I took care of her.

01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:44.791
And time passed.

01:06:46.375 --> 01:06:47.708
And here we are.

01:07:44.375 --> 01:07:45.958
Do you even like mangoes?

01:07:50.500 --> 01:07:52.750
No. They're too sweet.

01:07:57.541 --> 01:07:59.875
-They are too sweet.
-Way too sweet.

01:09:07.041 --> 01:09:08.041
Lærke?

01:09:19.583 --> 01:09:22.541
JOAN ZEUTHEN
MISSED CALL

01:09:30.041 --> 01:09:34.708
HOW'S OUR PLAN WORKING OUT?
HAVE YOU PERSUADED HIM TO SIGN?

01:09:37.208 --> 01:09:39.208
I think I might just take the day off.

01:09:41.041 --> 01:09:43.791
Perhaps we could go
to that market you suggested?

01:09:44.791 --> 01:09:45.916
If you want to?

01:09:46.916 --> 01:09:48.583
You have a text message.

01:09:58.083 --> 01:09:59.708
So that was your plan all along?

01:10:03.541 --> 01:10:05.333
I didn't know how to tell you.

01:10:05.416 --> 01:10:09.583
I understand why Agnes finds it
difficult to share stuff with you.

01:10:11.625 --> 01:10:12.583
Tell her

01:10:13.125 --> 01:10:15.375
she's always welcome at our place.

01:10:18.458 --> 01:10:19.583
Have a safe trip.

01:10:31.958 --> 01:10:33.125
Mom?

01:10:35.583 --> 01:10:36.541
Hi, sweetie.

01:10:37.250 --> 01:10:38.291
Are you okay?

01:10:45.791 --> 01:10:48.166
We all do stupid things

01:10:48.250 --> 01:10:49.375
when we like someone.

01:10:54.125 --> 01:10:56.125
-Admit that you like him.
-No.

01:10:56.208 --> 01:10:58.333
-Say it. You need to do it.
-Stop.

01:11:01.250 --> 01:11:04.125
You always need to be
in control of everything.

01:11:04.208 --> 01:11:06.625
It's not about whether I like him or not.

01:11:07.375 --> 01:11:08.458
What's it about then?

01:11:11.708 --> 01:11:13.458
I'm just not relationship material.

01:11:16.416 --> 01:11:18.000
I'm the type you need to avoid.

01:11:22.166 --> 01:11:24.500
I don't make people happy.

01:11:46.125 --> 01:11:47.125
I've seen it.

01:11:49.666 --> 01:11:51.041
He looks very happy.

01:11:53.708 --> 01:11:54.541
Yeah.

01:11:59.375 --> 01:12:02.250
And if anyone can solve problems,
it's you.

01:12:03.541 --> 01:12:04.500
And you know it.

01:12:11.833 --> 01:12:13.041
And no matter what…

01:12:16.375 --> 01:12:17.625
you've given me

01:12:18.333 --> 01:12:20.333
one of the best vacations I've ever had.

01:12:22.041 --> 01:12:24.166
And you've definitely made me happy.

01:12:42.500 --> 01:12:43.333
Hola.

01:12:47.083 --> 01:12:48.000
Excuse me?

01:12:48.500 --> 01:12:49.916
No, forget it.

01:12:50.000 --> 01:12:51.666
No, that's my seat,

01:12:51.750 --> 01:12:53.458
and your bag's in my seat.

01:12:56.375 --> 01:12:57.333
Thank you.

01:12:58.625 --> 01:13:00.583
-Thank you very much.
-Sure.

01:13:01.208 --> 01:13:02.416
-Hi.
-Hi.

01:13:06.000 --> 01:13:07.208
Didn't you have a baby?

01:13:07.291 --> 01:13:08.916
-What?
-You had a baby with you?

01:13:10.041 --> 01:13:12.875
Oh, right. He's with his dad in Spain.

01:13:14.416 --> 01:13:16.083
Half Spanish, half Danish.

01:13:16.166 --> 01:13:17.375
-Interesting.
-Yeah.

01:13:17.458 --> 01:13:18.916
It can work out.

01:13:27.291 --> 01:13:28.416
What's up with you?

01:13:28.500 --> 01:13:29.541
Nothing.

01:13:29.625 --> 01:13:30.750
Doesn't seem like it.

01:13:32.041 --> 01:13:34.708
Can you relax a bit?
You haven't stopped all morning.

01:13:38.166 --> 01:13:39.375
Can you talk to me?

01:13:50.000 --> 01:13:50.916
Dammit!

01:13:52.291 --> 01:13:53.125
Alex!

01:13:55.291 --> 01:13:56.250
Alex.

01:14:26.458 --> 01:14:27.541
Tired, you know?

01:14:30.916 --> 01:14:31.750
And?

01:14:34.416 --> 01:14:36.250
Were you talking about me or you?

01:14:38.291 --> 01:14:40.083
You, obviously.

01:14:40.166 --> 01:14:42.041
Look at yourself, you look super old.

01:15:20.125 --> 01:15:20.958
Are you?

01:15:23.666 --> 01:15:24.875
Yes, of course.

01:15:37.375 --> 01:15:38.458
I'm gonna eat.

01:16:08.541 --> 01:16:09.750
Hi, gorgeous.

01:16:10.250 --> 01:16:11.333
What's up?

01:16:11.416 --> 01:16:12.416
The board sent them.

01:16:12.500 --> 01:16:14.166
I think we nailed it.

01:16:14.250 --> 01:16:15.583
But he wouldn't sign it.

01:16:15.666 --> 01:16:17.541
I got the contract this morning.

01:16:19.041 --> 01:16:21.041
I don't know what you did. It's amazing.

01:16:21.125 --> 01:16:22.291
He signed.

01:16:22.791 --> 01:16:26.583
We just need the final documents,
and then you're off to Málaga.

01:16:26.666 --> 01:16:29.166
It'll be sorted in a couple of weeks,

01:16:29.250 --> 01:16:31.458
then you'll zip down there,
tear it all down,

01:16:31.541 --> 01:16:33.208
build everything, decorate,

01:16:33.291 --> 01:16:34.875
train the staff, and open.

01:16:37.250 --> 01:16:38.083
Right.

01:16:39.375 --> 01:16:40.708
I have to go.

01:16:42.000 --> 01:16:42.875
But…

01:16:55.625 --> 01:16:57.583
TRIED CALLING. LEFT A MESSAGE.

01:16:57.666 --> 01:16:59.458
CALL ME. YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND…

01:16:59.541 --> 01:17:02.583
LET ME EXPLAIN.
IT WAS A WONDERFUL NIGHT. SORRY.

01:17:13.208 --> 01:17:14.958
-Hi there.
-Hi there.

01:17:17.208 --> 01:17:18.291
Hi.

01:17:18.958 --> 01:17:21.041
I've read the applications.
They're impeccable.

01:17:21.791 --> 01:17:25.083
Everything's by the book.
We can't contest a single thing.

01:17:25.166 --> 01:17:26.666
-May I?
-Sure.

01:17:26.750 --> 01:17:28.000
Where was I?

01:17:28.083 --> 01:17:29.458
I talked to the bank.

01:17:29.541 --> 01:17:32.000
Your friend owes them 4.9 million kroner.

01:17:34.000 --> 01:17:36.375
Unless he can conjure up the money,

01:17:36.458 --> 01:17:38.583
he has little chance of keeping the farm.

01:17:40.375 --> 01:17:42.833
Yeah. Right, I've said it. That was all.

01:17:45.583 --> 01:17:46.625
Thanks for trying.

01:17:46.708 --> 01:17:47.958
Sure. All good.

01:17:49.166 --> 01:17:50.208
How is she?

01:17:51.458 --> 01:17:52.625
I think she misses you.

01:17:52.708 --> 01:17:53.541
No.

01:17:54.708 --> 01:17:56.333
She probably just misses Málaga.

01:17:56.875 --> 01:17:58.041
Yeah, that too.

01:17:58.958 --> 01:18:00.333
I think she misses you too.

01:18:12.083 --> 01:18:14.083
Did you always breathe so heavily?

01:18:15.333 --> 01:18:16.208
What?

01:18:16.708 --> 01:18:18.083
Your breathing's heavy.

01:18:18.166 --> 01:18:19.000
What?

01:18:19.083 --> 01:18:20.875
Stop it. It's annoying.

01:18:20.958 --> 01:18:23.083
I can't stop breathing.
I breathe normally.

01:18:23.166 --> 01:18:24.291
You're wheezing.

01:18:24.375 --> 01:18:26.416
Okay. Listen. We're having a…

01:18:27.375 --> 01:18:28.333
gender…

01:18:29.458 --> 01:18:31.166
re… reveal.

01:18:31.250 --> 01:18:32.500
You're having a what?

01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:34.583
-We're having a--
-A what?

01:18:34.666 --> 01:18:36.083
…gender reveal.

01:18:37.041 --> 01:18:39.250
A baby shower, kind of… I guess.

01:18:39.333 --> 01:18:41.208
A gender reveal?

01:18:41.708 --> 01:18:43.166
Baby shower? Really?

01:18:43.250 --> 01:18:44.791
Vivi really wants one.

01:18:44.875 --> 01:18:46.125
-She does?
-Yes.

01:18:46.208 --> 01:18:47.625
-Do you want to come?
-No.

01:18:48.333 --> 01:18:50.291
-For Agnes' sake?
-No.

01:18:51.166 --> 01:18:52.833
For Agnes and for me,

01:18:52.916 --> 01:18:54.375
and just very briefly?

01:18:56.833 --> 01:18:57.666
Thanks.

01:18:59.333 --> 01:19:00.791
I can tell. Thanks.

01:19:00.875 --> 01:19:02.125
Can I have the bottle?

01:19:03.583 --> 01:19:05.083
It's Vivi, you know.

01:19:05.791 --> 01:19:07.958
It'd be nice for her
just to have one glass.

01:19:08.041 --> 01:19:09.000
Just take it.

01:19:10.250 --> 01:19:11.083
Thanks.

01:19:13.666 --> 01:19:14.791
By the way,

01:19:15.291 --> 01:19:18.333
he has a 14-day withdrawal period,
if need be.

01:19:18.416 --> 01:19:19.250
Okay?

01:19:19.958 --> 01:19:21.416
-See you.
-Thanks for helping.

01:19:22.375 --> 01:19:23.208
Gender.

01:19:31.041 --> 01:19:34.041
SHOULD WE SELL YOUR HOUSE TOO?
APPRAISAL FREE OF CHARGE SOLD!

01:19:34.125 --> 01:19:36.166
Three, two, one!

01:19:45.541 --> 01:19:46.958
That was perfect.

01:19:47.041 --> 01:19:48.333
Another little girl.

01:19:49.916 --> 01:19:51.166
Awesome.

01:19:52.875 --> 01:19:54.500
Please, dig in.

01:20:51.708 --> 01:20:52.708
Are you snooping?

01:20:54.500 --> 01:20:56.791
No. I'm not. Um…

01:20:57.541 --> 01:20:58.666
Is that your project?

01:20:59.166 --> 01:21:00.208
Yes.

01:21:00.291 --> 01:21:01.541
it is.

01:21:02.166 --> 01:21:03.375
How does it work?

01:21:03.875 --> 01:21:06.125
-You don't have to ask.
-But I'd like to know.

01:21:13.666 --> 01:21:16.250
-You know what tiny houses are, don't you?
-Yes.

01:21:17.375 --> 01:21:20.875
So, everyone's got their own household.

01:21:22.791 --> 01:21:24.875
And then you share the big expenses,

01:21:24.958 --> 01:21:25.958
such as…

01:21:26.708 --> 01:21:28.333
solar panels,

01:21:28.416 --> 01:21:31.416
geothermal heating or wind,
depending on where you live.

01:21:31.500 --> 01:21:34.000
Shared water supply and heating system.

01:21:34.500 --> 01:21:38.041
The houses are, of course,
built from biogenic materials.

01:21:38.125 --> 01:21:40.208
Preferably regenerative.

01:21:40.833 --> 01:21:43.791
The walls are made of rammed clay soil

01:21:43.875 --> 01:21:45.500
and insulated with seagrass,

01:21:45.583 --> 01:21:47.000
and there's shingle roofs

01:21:47.083 --> 01:21:49.833
made from wood scraps to make it

01:21:49.916 --> 01:21:52.750
dynamic and environmentally friendly and…

01:21:59.750 --> 01:22:00.750
What?

01:22:05.791 --> 01:22:07.083
It's just a great idea.

01:22:09.666 --> 01:22:10.708
And it's yours.

01:22:11.458 --> 01:22:14.333
Thanks.
Tell the school of architecture that.

01:22:14.833 --> 01:22:16.041
Fuck that school.

01:22:16.125 --> 01:22:16.958
Yeah.

01:22:17.541 --> 01:22:18.416
Fuck it.

01:22:21.250 --> 01:22:22.541
Have you talked to Paula?

01:22:23.041 --> 01:22:25.416
-Yeah. We've been texting.
-Yeah?

01:22:28.541 --> 01:22:29.625
Have you talked to Alex?

01:22:29.708 --> 01:22:32.125
Um… no.

01:22:34.208 --> 01:22:35.916
I think the reception's quite bad.

01:22:37.583 --> 01:22:38.541
Just call him.

01:22:46.583 --> 01:22:47.416
There's cake.

01:22:47.500 --> 01:22:49.125
Right. I'll be right down.

01:23:09.250 --> 01:23:10.208
Agnes!

01:23:13.125 --> 01:23:14.041
Come here, please.

01:23:17.333 --> 01:23:18.208
What's up?

01:23:23.291 --> 01:23:24.291
Pack your bag.

01:23:30.750 --> 01:23:32.083
Are you stupid?

01:23:33.208 --> 01:23:34.500
Yes, maybe.

01:23:34.583 --> 01:23:37.833
-We'll build without you.
-You won't build that hotel.

01:23:37.916 --> 01:23:39.666
Perhaps somewhere else, but not…

01:23:40.833 --> 01:23:42.333
not in that orchard.

01:23:42.416 --> 01:23:43.416
What can you do?

01:23:43.500 --> 01:23:47.333
-We have a contract. He signed.
-But he has 14 days to cancel.

01:23:52.666 --> 01:23:54.166
So you want to stop this?

01:23:54.250 --> 01:23:55.458
You don't have to understand.

01:23:57.666 --> 01:23:59.791
I'm grateful for everything.

01:23:59.875 --> 01:24:01.208
I'm so sorry,

01:24:01.291 --> 01:24:03.000
but this is the way it has to be.

01:24:04.583 --> 01:24:05.750
I have to do this.

01:24:16.833 --> 01:24:17.750
You're fired.

01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:21.875
Yes.

01:24:23.166 --> 01:24:24.208
Shit!

01:24:42.541 --> 01:24:43.458
Good, and you?

01:25:08.333 --> 01:25:09.458
Why are you here?

01:25:09.958 --> 01:25:10.875
Can we talk?

01:25:13.500 --> 01:25:17.333
-There's nothing to talk about.
-Five minutes and I'll let you be.

01:25:17.416 --> 01:25:19.125
I have to bring in the harvest.

01:25:19.208 --> 01:25:22.083
And we have nothing to talk about. Okay?

01:25:29.291 --> 01:25:30.125
Fine.

01:25:59.875 --> 01:26:00.708
Yeah.

01:26:01.750 --> 01:26:02.833
They'll be fine.

01:26:34.416 --> 01:26:35.875
-Are we done?
-Yes.

01:26:36.416 --> 01:26:39.083
-Can we talk now?
-We have to move all the crates.

01:26:40.958 --> 01:26:41.791
Help me.

01:26:43.041 --> 01:26:43.875
Thank you.

01:26:51.416 --> 01:26:52.291
Come on.

01:27:12.041 --> 01:27:13.916
We're just standing here. Listen.

01:27:14.000 --> 01:27:14.833
I'm working.

01:27:14.916 --> 01:27:18.541
It's not insulin, it's mangoes.
Please just hear me out?

01:27:18.625 --> 01:27:19.916
-What--
-It's diffi--

01:27:20.000 --> 01:27:20.833
Then tell me!

01:27:20.916 --> 01:27:24.291
It's difficult to apologize
when I'm yelling at you.

01:27:25.750 --> 01:27:26.875
But I'm sorry!

01:27:28.791 --> 01:27:32.208
I'm sorry I didn't do better.
I tried, but it went so wrong.

01:27:32.291 --> 01:27:33.416
You did great.

01:27:34.000 --> 01:27:35.416
You got what you wanted.

01:27:35.958 --> 01:27:39.500
You've bought the place.
You'll get your shiny hotel. It's perfect.

01:27:42.875 --> 01:27:43.875
Why are you here?

01:27:45.500 --> 01:27:46.541
Because of you.

01:27:49.541 --> 01:27:50.625
I'm here because of you.

01:27:56.291 --> 01:27:58.041
You don't need to sell to Weltzer.

01:27:59.083 --> 01:28:00.666
-What?
-I've sold my apartment.

01:28:00.750 --> 01:28:02.208
And I've borrowed some money.

01:28:03.208 --> 01:28:04.791
Quite a lot of money, actually.

01:28:05.791 --> 01:28:06.916
Way too much money.

01:28:15.500 --> 01:28:17.125
You've sold your apartment?

01:28:18.583 --> 01:28:19.666
Yes.

01:28:22.625 --> 01:28:23.916
You have huge debts.

01:28:24.583 --> 01:28:25.416
Yeah.

01:28:27.791 --> 01:28:28.958
You have no assets?

01:28:30.166 --> 01:28:31.041
Nope.

01:28:33.833 --> 01:28:34.958
What's your plan?

01:28:52.708 --> 01:28:58.875
12 MONTHS LATER

01:29:04.083 --> 01:29:04.916
Dude!

01:29:20.291 --> 01:29:22.541
-Beautiful.
-Hi.

01:29:22.625 --> 01:29:23.500
Hola, chica.

01:29:23.583 --> 01:29:24.541
Hola, chica.

01:29:28.875 --> 01:29:30.250
It looks pretty good, huh?

01:29:33.750 --> 01:29:35.041
You look pretty good.

01:29:37.625 --> 01:29:38.500
Are you proud?

01:29:40.333 --> 01:29:41.416
Yes. Very.

01:29:44.000 --> 01:29:45.833
-Are you crying?
-What?

01:29:45.916 --> 01:29:48.291
-Are you crying?
-Am I crying? No way!

01:29:48.375 --> 01:29:50.791
Are you so proud that you're crying?

01:29:51.416 --> 01:29:52.750
-Just a little?
-No.

01:29:52.833 --> 01:29:53.708
Let me see.

01:29:55.291 --> 01:29:56.666
-Wet eyes--
-It's sweat.

01:29:56.750 --> 01:29:58.291
-Eye sweat--
-I'm sweating.

01:30:10.041 --> 01:30:12.083
-We need to talk about something.
-Okay?

01:30:15.708 --> 01:30:18.041
Mangonade can't be on the menu.
Nobody gets it!

01:30:18.125 --> 01:30:20.500
Everybody gets it once you explain it.

01:30:20.583 --> 01:30:21.958
-Lemonade, mangonade.
-But--

01:30:22.041 --> 01:30:23.625
We're also adding avocade.

01:30:23.708 --> 01:30:24.750
-What? No.
-Avocade.

01:30:24.833 --> 01:30:27.875
From avocado. So it'll be
lemonade, mangonade, avocade. Wow.

01:30:28.750 --> 01:30:29.708
Great idea, right?

01:30:32.125 --> 01:30:35.208
That will never happen!

01:34:31.166 --> 01:34:36.166
Subtitle translation by:
Toke Lasvill-Andersen
